local _,A=...
A.ReleaseNotes={version="1.2.6",changes={"Open the coin purse on the map to find nearby repairers, vendors, trainers, innkeepers, flight masters and mailboxes. Check the distance and click a result to navigate.","Expand a category to browse goods by icon, see who sells an item or find another provider. Search by item, service or NPC name. Vendor and trainer locations come with Mapperly.","Destinations, Notes, Filters and Settings now open beside the map at the same width as Nearby Services and the quest log. Switch tools without resizing the map canvas.","Preview a route beside the map and go back to its destination. Notes shows all twelve symbols together, Settings uses shorter pages, and long lists expand with the map.","Long routes use precomputed walking connections and check walking and transport options earlier. The planner skips disconnected ground and avoids repeating failed searches.","Cross more bridges within and between zones, including the Southfury bridge, the Westfall to Duskwood bridge and the northern Stranglethorn road to Duskwood.","Verified bridge decks now guide you through narrow or tilted crossings. Mapperly checks both approaches, avoids unproven shortcuts and handles journeys starting on a deck.","Walk through all four Dun Algaz tunnels between Loch Modan and the Wetlands. The arrow follows the tunnel to its far exit even when the zone changes underground.","If planning fails, choose Copy report and press Ctrl+C (Cmd+C on Mac) to share the attempt in Mapperly's CurseForge comments. Reports include the destination, settings and timings.","Follow a continuous world-map line with rounded bends and a consistent width as you zoom. Completed sections fade, transport legs use blue dots and the minimap shows one cue ahead.","In Settings > Navigation > Display > Route style, change the colours ahead and behind you, line width and direction markers on both maps. A live preview shows your choices.","Hover a zone or city on the continent map to see its minimum and recommended fishing skill where known. Larger text and a shorter tooltip make the guidance easier to read."}}
